{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final LDAP record contains the supplied Morgan Lake attributes, while hr.ldif remains at the required path with its original 201-byte size and baseline SHA-256 hash.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2e5c243ab934eff","seeded-state-node1"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the directory-reader identity to search employee names and mail addresses from node2 while preventing it from reading employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An authenticated reader search from node2 returned Morgan Lake and the mail address but no employeeNumber, both before and after node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-16036a296a3b4e2d","cmd-001a544555684c50"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Permit only the HR administrator to read or change employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persisted ACL grants the administrator write access and denies all others; the reader's modification received insufficient-access error 50, while the administrator successfully read, changed, verified, and restored the value to HR-4815.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2e5c243ab934eff","cmd-16036a296a3b4e2d","cmd-707e9942932547f7"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Prevent anonymous users from seeing employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous employee searches from node2 returned zero records before and after restart, consistent with the persisted subtree ACL denying all unspecified identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-16036a296a3b4e2d","cmd-001a544555684c50","cmd-a2e5c243ab934eff"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the reader and administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated administrator and directory-reader DNs were configured, successful binds demonstrate working credentials, and root-owned mode-600 credential artifacts persisted on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15eaa6bd7bc44375","cmd-0025998701244549","cmd-001a544555684c50"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210. OpenLDAP 2.4.42 packages from the Xenial repositories were installed and remained operational after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2e5c243ab934eff","cmd-001a544555684c50","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, credential and ACL creation, data loading, node-to-node credential provisioning, bounded access-control tests, restoration of the temporary administrator test value, and required restarts all had clear roles. Temporary test files were removed, package health remained clean, and neither node had failed services afterward. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart scheduling, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered LDAP service, data, credentials, and cross-node access.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9dffaf56f024f6a","cmd-5f210abd6e794475","cmd-b71b1810cf2b4a6e","cmd-552b6ff98b504883","cmd-ba9c2db5cc1348aa","cmd-16036a296a3b4e2d","cmd-707e9942932547f7","cmd-536a112fa28a4469","cmd-5a69a37290ea41bd","cmd-74ebfe0d48434065","cmd-001a544555684c50","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. Field-level LDAP privacy works from node2, anonymous access is denied, the supplied data and protected demonstration credentials persist, and the legacy OS/kernel were retained. Restart evidence is complete and coherent for both managed nodes.","limitations":[]}
